Keyword leg: query the root copies of the nested text fields

The hybrid search's keyword leg is a plain multi_match on titles.title,
descriptions.description and subjects.subject. In the metadata warehouse's
OpenSearch mapping these are nested, so the query never matches and ranking
comes from the kNN leg alone. The mapping copies each of them (copy_to) into
a root text field, _title, _description and _subject; query those, as the
creator filter already does with _creator.

Applies to data-commons-search v0.10.2 (6c07bdc33a29c91cde58082c068c107872b75733);
main has the same code.

--- a/src/data_commons_search/mcp_server.py
+++ b/src/data_commons_search/mcp_server.py
@@ -283,11 +283,13 @@ async def _search_data_one(
     keyword_query: dict[str, Any] = {
         "multi_match": {
             "query": search_input,
+            # titles, descriptions and subjects are nested, which a plain multi_match never
+            # matches: query their root copies (copy_to in the warehouse's mapping), as _creator
             "fields": [
                 # "titles.title^2",
-                "titles.title",
-                "descriptions.description",
-                "subjects.subject",
+                "_title",
+                "_description",
+                "_subject",
                 # "subjects.subject^1.5",
                 # TODO: add more fields?
             ],
